{
  "slug": "fhir-format",
  "name": "Fhir Format",
  "type": "plugin",
  "description": "Accuracy-first FHIR R4/R4B/R5 skill for JSON formatting and reasoning. It labels claims as normative/version-delta/profile-dependent/practice, requires source-backed normative statements, avoids guessed terminology codes, and clearly separates structural validation from full profile conformance.",
  "longDescription": "Ships **1 skill**, `fhir-format` (Accuracy-first specialist for FHIR R4/R4B/R5 JSON, profile-aware guidance, and non-fabricated terminology and integration support).\n\nInstalls with `claude plugin install fhir-format@claude-community` from `dnlbox/fhir-format-skill`.\n\nA Claude plugin for sourced FHIR guidance. Not a FHIR development assistant — a reasoning layer that keeps the agent honest about what the spec actually says.",
  "compatibility": [
    "claude",
    "copilot",
    "antigravity",
